---
title: "Quickstart"
description: "Get QQL running in under 60 seconds — connect to Qdrant, create a collection, insert documents, and run your first search."
sidebar:
  order: 3
---

Get from zero to your first search result in under 60 seconds.

## 1. Start Qdrant

{% terminal title="Start Qdrant" %}
docker run -p 6333:6333 -p 6334:6334 qdrant/qdrant
{% /terminal %}

Or use a [Qdrant Cloud](https://cloud.qdrant.io/) cluster.

## 2. Connect

**Local Qdrant (no inference):**

{% terminal title="Local" %}
qql-go connect --url http://localhost:6334
{% /terminal %}

**Qdrant Cloud:**

{% terminal title="Cloud" %}
qql-go connect --url https://<cluster>.qdrant.io --secret <api-key>
{% /terminal %}

**Local with embeddings (local inference mode):**

{% terminal title="Local inference" %}
qql-go connect \
  --url http://localhost:6334 \
  --inference-mode local \
  --embedding-endpoint http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1/embeddings \
  --embedding-model text-embedding-all-minilm-l6-v2-embedding
{% /terminal %}

Verify the connection:

{% terminal title="Verify" %}
qql-go doctor
{% /terminal %}

## 3. Create a Collection

{% terminal title="Create collection" %}
qql-go exec "CREATE COLLECTION docs HYBRID"
{% /terminal %}

{% aside type="tip" title="Collection types" %}
The `HYBRID` keyword creates a collection with both dense and sparse vector support.
{% /aside %}

With HNSW tuning and quantization:

{% terminal title="Advanced collection" %}
qql-go exec "CREATE COLLECTION docs HYBRID WITH HNSW (m = 32, ef_construct = 100) WITH QUANTIZATION (type = 'scalar')"
{% /terminal %}

## 4. Create Payload Indexes

Always create indexes on fields you'll filter on:

{% terminal title="Indexes" %}
qql-go exec "CREATE INDEX ON docs FOR category TYPE keyword"
qql-go exec "CREATE INDEX ON docs FOR year TYPE integer"
{% /terminal %}

## 5. Insert Documents

{% terminal title="Insert" %}
qql-go exec "INSERT INTO docs VALUES {'id': 1, 'text': 'Qdrant stores dense and sparse vectors', 'category': 'search'} USING HYBRID"
qql-go exec "INSERT INTO docs VALUES {'id': 2, 'text': 'QQL makes vector search feel like SQL', 'category': 'tooling'} USING HYBRID"
qql-go exec "INSERT INTO docs VALUES {'id': 3, 'text': 'Hybrid search combines dense and BM25 sparse signals', 'category': 'search'} USING HYBRID"
{% /terminal %}

{% aside type="note" title="Batch inserts" %}
You can also batch multiple documents in a single statement for better performance.
{% /aside %}

Batch insert multiple documents in one statement:

{% terminal title="Batch insert" %}
qql-go exec "INSERT INTO docs VALUES {'id': 4, 'text': 'Qdrant supports HNSW indexing'}, {'id': 5, 'text': 'Score boosting with BOOST expressions'} USING HYBRID"
{% /terminal %}

## 6. Search

{% terminal title="Search examples" %}
qql-go exec "QUERY 'vector database' FROM docs LIMIT 5"
qql-go exec "QUERY 'vector database' FROM docs LIMIT 5 USING HYBRID"
qql-go exec "QUERY 'search' FROM docs LIMIT 5 WHERE category = 'search'"
{% /terminal %}

## 7. Explain a Query (without executing)

{% terminal title="Explain" %}
qql-go explain "QUERY 'vector database' FROM docs LIMIT 5 USING HYBRID RERANK"
{% /terminal %}

## 8. Explore with the REPL

{% terminal title="REPL" %}
qql-go repl
{% /terminal %}

{% aside type="tip" title="REPL tips" %}
The REPL supports tab completion and multi-line statements.
{% /aside %}

---

## Common Next Steps

| Goal | Command |
|---|---|
| Show all collections | `qql-go exec "SHOW COLLECTIONS"` |
| Collection details | `qql-go exec "SHOW COLLECTION docs"` |
| Structured JSON output | `qql-go exec --quiet --json "SHOW COLLECTIONS"` |
| Browse all points | `qql-go exec "SCROLL FROM docs LIMIT 20"` |
| Delete a collection | `qql-go exec "DROP COLLECTION docs"` |

